 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "7:11-15 is not glossed (Al-Muyassar keeps the first person «آياتنا»). The Fire (8) and Paradise (9-10) are never drawn: geometric and light moods, no river; a lamp for «يهديهم ربهم», light for «الحمد لله رب العالمين». Night and day for «اختلاف الليل والنهار», stars for the heavens, wind for the fleeting life. STAGING v4: The old chapter 7-8 is split (owner rule: an unseen verse is ambient). c1 (6) stays ambient: night and day and what He created (His acts); quiet over 6:6-11. c2 (7) is staged in a market by day: two small groups of three men (blamed, so no woman is drawn; the second walks in on 7:1) trade and talk with each other on 7:6 and 7:8 (content with this world, both tafsirs), sit down at ease on 7:9-10 (As-Sa'di: they relied on it), and on the signs (7:12-14, Al-Muyassar: the signs in creation and the revealed ones) a few birds cross the sky while one group turns its back (7:15, heedless). Nobody gestures in the negated clause 7:1-5. A coins plate for this world's life (7:7). c3 (8, new title) is ambient on a night sky: their abode in the Fire, never drawn, no plate. c4 (9-10) stays ambient (Paradise): no river or garden; the plates are now geometric (a light plate starting on His guiding, 9:6, or one word before the Name, 10:11, reads as Him appearing as light), and the background stays quiet over 9:6-8 and verse 10 (their glorification and the greeting, which Al-Muyassar gives as from Allah and His angels)."
 },
